> > What is the "protection racket"?
>
> It's an often debated strategy that offers some rewards at potentially high
> costs, but, according to its defenders, also has the advantage of teaching you
> useful tactics. In a nutshell:
>
> Let your pet do all the fighting, but mostly run away from monsters, straight
> down into the gnomish mines and to minetown, grabbing all the gold you can on
> the way (possibly by stealing from shops in between). Arrive at the minetown
> temple while preferrably still at XL1

FWIW although I've argued strongly against it as a high-percentage
strategy, I do think newer players should give it a try until they can
pull it off with some success (say, 40% of the time) just to learn the
concepts involved.  It's an excellent way to break out of the hack-and-
slash mentality.


